from pathlib import Path
import json,html,re
out=Path('responsive-header-audit');records=json.loads((out/'headers-before.json').read_text());(out/'changed-header-pages.json').write_text(json.dumps([r['page'] for r in records],indent=2));widths=[320,375,390,430,650,680,768,900,1024,1280,1366,1440,1920];sections=''
for w in widths:
 states=[('closed','Closed header')]+([('menu','Open MENU — nine categories and contact utility'),('buy','Buy expanded inline — other categories remain visible')] if w<1280 else [('buy','Buy — five priorities'),('design','Interior Design'),('life','Life Changes'),('sell','Sell'),('management','Property Management'),('contact','Contact'),('buy-flyout-0','Buying Process flyout'),('buy-flyout-1','Financing flyout'),('buy-flyout-2','Buyer Resources flyout')])+[('neighborhoods','Neighborhoods — 30 direct city and regional links'),('search','Search — actual personalized search experience')]
 figures=''.join('<figure><figcaption>'+html.escape(label)+'</figcaption><a href="'+str(w)+'-'+state+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+str(w)+'-'+state+'.png" alt="'+html.escape(label)+' at '+str(w)+' CSS pixels"></a></figure>' for state,label in states)
 sections+='<section class="previews" data-width="'+str(w)+'"'+(' hidden' if w!=768 else '')+'><h2>'+str(w)+' CSS pixels</h2><div class="gallery">'+figures+'</div></section>'
comp=''
for w in [650,1366]:
 comp+='<h3>'+str(w)+'px — matching viewport comparison</h3><div class="gallery comparisons">'+''.join('<figure><figcaption>'+label+' — header detail; click for full screenshot</figcaption><a href="'+prefix+str(w)+'-closed.png"><img src="'+prefix+str(w)+'-closed.png" alt="'+label+' header at '+str(w)+' pixels"></a></figure>' for prefix,label in [('before/','Before'),('','After')])+'</div>'
(out/'review.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>DommyDom · responsive header and open menu review</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f8f7f3;color:#343c32;font:15px/1.65 Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;color:#48533e}p{max-width:1080px}a{color:#48533e}.notice{padding:16px;border-left:4px solid #48533e;background:#fff}.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;align-items:start}figure{margin:0}figcaption{font-weight:600;padding:12px 0}img{display:block;max-width:100%;width:auto;height:auto;border:1px solid #d8dbd0}.comparisons img{width:100%;height:190px;object-fit:cover;object-position:top}select{padding:10px 16px;font:inherit;color:#48533e;border:1px solid #48533e;background:white}table{border-collapse:collapse;background:white;margin:20px 0}td,th{padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8dbd0;text-align:left}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}details{margin:28px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;color:#48533e}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.comparisons img{height:145px}}</style><main><h1>DommyDom · header and open menu repair</h1><p class="notice"><strong>Local owner review.</strong> No commits, pushes, publishing, or deployment.</p><p>The header now has two deliberate bands. Full desktop groups the signature and RISE marks together, places the two phone links and email in a compact contact area, and keeps Neighborhoods/Search together at the right. The second tier has exactly nine primary categories on one centered line. Compact views use a brand band and an evenly distributed Neighborhoods/Search/MENU band; contact details appear inside the open MENU.</p><p><strong>Measured heights:</strong> approximately 137px on full desktop, 132px on tablet and most phones, and 116px at 320px. The previous 650px header was 174px tall; its replacement is 132px. The previous 1366px header was 157px; its replacement is 137px. This repair adds no third contact band.</p><p><strong>Open MENU:</strong> one bounded ivory surface, no wider than 480px, aligned to MENU and the right page gutter. All nine primary categories appear in one column, followed by the original telephone/email utility. Tapping a category expands its relevant links inline and preserves the other primary categories; tapping it again collapses it. The Close control remains in the header, and the panel scrolls independently when expanded content needs room.</p><p>Buy stays concise on compact screens: its five priority destinations and the existing California homebuyer-programs link. It uses existing meaningful content landing pages instead of pre-expanding every article or adding another accordion. Every process, financing, and buyer-question article is retained on its existing landing page; desktop hover flyouts still expose those direct article links. Parent category destinations remain available within their inline panels.</p><p><strong>Neighborhoods and Search:</strong> both open automatically on desktop hover, over the icon or text; touch uses a tap. All 26 cities and four regional guides are direct links. Search retains its genuine <a href="../search.html">Personalized Home Search</a> option. No fake filters, directory pages, or extra main categories were added.</p><details><summary>Root causes and implementation</summary><p>The active homepage cascade contained 176 header rules, including conflicting fixed heights, contact-strip positioning, and breakpoint overrides. The previous controller measured only navigation fit. A separate legacy filename selector also capped the signature at 72px on some content pages, while the global button skin moved and colored hover controls.</p><p>The repaired header uses isolated <code>dd-*</code> hooks so legacy <code>ss22-*</code> restoration rules no longer control it. Its shared stylesheet was replaced, not appended with another repeated-ID override. Targeted component resets contain the old global button skin, font reset, and key-icon size cap. Full-mode fit measures both utility zones and navigation spacing.</p><p><strong>Breakpoints:</strong> 1280px is the tested minimum for the full composition, with a measured fallback to MENU if either utility or nav spacing fails. Below 1280px the layout always uses the two-band compact design. At 600px and below, signature/RISE and action sizes adapt for phones. Desktop content is capped at 1440px with controlled gutters; compact MENU is capped at 480px.</p><p><strong>Changed files:</strong> header markup in all 351 live HTML pages; <code>assets/responsive-navigation.css</code>, <code>assets/navigation-v22.js</code>, and <code>assets/v46-mobile-menu.js</code>. The sole change to <code>assets/home-hero-fit.js</code> is its header lookup, retaining the existing header-height measurement and hero algorithm. <a href="changed-header-pages.json">Complete HTML file list</a>.</p><p>All bodies and head/SEO markup are byte-preserved. Existing image and video assets, article cards, city content, copy, dates, and page URLs are retained. All 89 existing header page destinations and 30 Neighborhoods links resolve; all original header link labels and destinations are unchanged in source. <a href="source-verification.json">Full preservation and URL audit</a>.</p></details><p><strong>Validation:</strong> six page types at thirteen real CSS viewport widths (78 combinations): homepage, Buy, Sell, Life Changes, city, and Blog. All ten mandatory widths are included, plus 375px, 430px, and the 680px acceptance preview. Tests cover open MENU, contacts, inline expansion, all dropdowns/flyouts, hover transfer, keyboard/Escape, touch, direct nested-page navigation, resizing and scroll restoration. These are local Chrome screenshots with touch emulation, not physical-device testing. External integrations were blocked and no forms were submitted.</p><p><a href="browser-results.json">Layout and menu results</a> · <a href="interaction-results.json">Navigation and interaction results</a> · <a href="source-verification.json">Source and URL audit</a></p><h2>Before and after</h2>'''+comp+'''<h2>Inspect every viewport and open state</h2><label for="width">CSS viewport width </label><select id="width">'''+''.join('<option'+(' selected' if w==768 else '')+'>'+str(w)+'</option>' for w in widths)+'''</select><p>Each screenshot is labeled. Click for the original full-size capture.</p>'''+sections+'''<script>document.querySelector('#width').addEventListener('change',e=>document.querySelectorAll('.previews').forEach(s=>s.hidden=s.dataset.width!==e.target.value));</script></main></html>''',encoding='utf-8');print('Created labeled review gallery and before/after comparisons.')
